# Feed the Swarm's other target kind: "enchantment an opponent controls". Bot2's Assault Formation (a noncreature
# enchantment, mana value 2) is destroyed and Bot1 loses 2 life (20 -> 18), twice what the Elves cost in the creature
# scenario, so the life lost follows the permanent's mana value and not a fixed amount.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Feed the Swarm
Swamp x18

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Mox Emerald
Assault Formation
Forest x17

[Actions]
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Assault Formation.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Black)
Bot1.Hand.Feed the Swarm.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Assault Formation)

[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 18
Bot2.Life = 20
Bot2.Graveyard = Assault Formation
Bot2.Battlefield = Forest; Mox Emerald
Bot1.Graveyard = Feed the Swarm; Black Lotus
